%description:
NR AM max-retransmission -> radio-link-failure indication (TS 38.322 5.3.2): when
RETX_COUNT reaches maxRetxThreshold the AM entity shall indicate to upper layers that the
maximum number of retransmissions has been reached (RRC uses this to declare RLF).

FAITHFUL ASSERTION: under sustained loss that trips maxRetxThreshold, an RLF/max-retx
indication becomes observable to the rest of the stack (here: a "radioLinkFailure" signal
at the RLC/RRC boundary).

[NOT-MODELED] Simu5G detects the condition but only sets a private bool
(AmTxQueue::radioLinkFailureDetected_) and calls BearerManagement::scheduleRadioLinkFailure()
directly; it emits NO signal and sends NO indication PDU (RLC-spec-gap-analysis.md #1). So
the faithful assertion cannot be satisfied and the program FAILs -> EXPECTEDFAIL. RLF is
observable in Simu5G only via side effects (the AM entity + PDCP modules getting deleted,
traffic going silent). This test documents the gap; if an RLF indication signal is added,
it flips to PASS.

A degraded channel (low power, far UE, high target BLER) is configured so retransmissions
accumulate toward maxRetxThreshold within the run.

%file: Nr_Am_MaxRetxRlf.cc

#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "Simu5gRlcTestSupport.h"

namespace inet { namespace protocoltest {

using namespace rlctest;

Define_ProtocolTest(nr_am_maxretx_rlf)
{
    return ProtocolTest("nr_am_maxretx_rlf")
        // Sanity: the DL AM TX (on the gNB) is actually retransmitting.
        .once(on("gnb.cellularNic").signal("retransmissionPdu").within(2.5)
                  .describe("at least one AM retransmission occurs"))
        // Faithful: an RLF / max-retx indication is surfaced. No such signal exists today.
        .once(on("gnb.cellularNic").signal("radioLinkFailure").within(2.5)
                  .describe("an RLF indication reaches upper layers"));
}

} } // namespace

%inifile: test.ini
[General]
include ../../ini/_nr.ini
*.tester.testName = "nr_am_maxretx_rlf"
**.cellularNic.ip2nic.conversationalRlc = "AM"

# Degraded uplink/downlink so PDUs are lost and retransmissions pile up.
**.eNodeBTxPower = 5dBm
**.ueTxPower = 2dBm
**.targetBler = 0.3
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 950m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 900m
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 100B

%expected-failure: Simu5G NR AM does not indicate RLF/max-retx to upper layers (RLC-spec-gap-analysis.md #1) -- NOT-MODELED

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST nr_am_maxretx_rlf: PASS
